<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n81778" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περίοιδα</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιήδη</span></b> , pf. and plpf. (in
		pres. and impf. sense), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>know well</i>, c. inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περίοιδε νοῆσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.247
				</span></i>
			 : c. dat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴχνεσι γὰρ
			περιῄδη</span> for he <i>was very skilled in</i> the tracks,
				<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.317
			</span></i> : c.acc. rei et gen. pers., <i>know better than</i>
			others, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περίοιδε δίκας ἠδὲ φρόνιν ἄλλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.244
				</span></i>
			 (nisi leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ</span>
			(Adv.) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶδε</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; βουλῇ περιίδμεναι ἄλλων</span>
			<i>to be better skilled in</i> counsel than others, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.728
			</span></i>.</div>
